@startuml
title D-02 Assisted Payment Terminal Operating Modes

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

component "Assisted Payment Terminal\none terminal app family" as APT
component "Mode 1:\nCashier-Assisted Terminal" as Cashier
component "Mode 2:\nContinuity Terminal" as Continuity
component "Normal staffed operation" as Normal
component "Approved degraded / BCP operation" as BCP
component "Central PMS" as Central
component "Resolved Site POS Server" as POS
component "Operator Console /\napproved operations workflow" as Console

APT --> Cashier
APT --> Continuity
Cashier --> Normal : enabled for staffed payment
Continuity --> BCP : disabled by default
Cashier --> Central : session, payable basis,\npayment status
Cashier --> POS : fiscal routing through backend flow
Continuity --> Central : controlled degraded workflow
Continuity --> POS : fiscal routing where available and allowed
Continuity --> Console : approval, incident,\naudit, reconciliation

note bottom of APT
Operator Console is a separate non-payment module.
The terminal app family is payment-capable but not finality authority.
end note

@enduml
